    },
    "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ be open, with the standard Euclidean metric and orientation. Let $a\\in W^{1,2}_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega;\\mathfrak{su}(2)\\otimes\\mathbb R^4)$ satisfy $d^*a=0$ and $F_a^+=0$ distributionally, where $F_a=da+a\\wedge a$ and $F_a^+=(F_a+*F_a)/2$. Then the coefficient classes of $a$ have smooth representatives on $\\Omega$, and these representatives satisfy the same equations classically.\n\nThis is an interior assertion for a given weak Coulomb gauge. No boundary regularity, existence of a gauge, curved-metric or perturbed ASD equation, singular removal, Fredholm statement, or gluing theorem is asserted.",
    "raw_sha256": "c797668194bbcd4ee125596de76fc1cffbf417b4bbf67437169d5affe2d3fddc"
